1:/* cave_fade.h â€” NES cave entry / exit Link-descend animation.
2: *
3: * Matches NES Z_05.asm:2308 UpdateMode10Stairs_Full + InitMode10
4: * (Z_05.asm:1400). NES sequence on entry:
5: *   1. Link standing on entrance tile $24 (or stairs $70-$73, $88).
6: *   2. EffectRequest = $08 (stairs effect), StairsTargetY = ObjY + $10.
7: *   3. Each frame: every 4th frame (FrameCounter & 3 == 0), increment
8: *      ObjY by 1 (Link walks down one pixel). 16 px total = 64 frames.
9: *      Link upper-half sprites get priority bit $20 set so background
10: *      entrance arch covers them ("Link sinks into hole" effect).
11: *   4. When ObjY == StairsTargetY: GameMode = TargetMode (cave). Scene
12: *      swaps instantly to cave with Link at bottom-center.
13: *
14: * Exit mirrors with ObjY -= 1 every 4 frames until target reached.
15: * For Tier 1 simplicity, exit uses a snap (no ascend anim) â€” user
16: * hits C+START chord to leave; Link snaps to OW return position.
17: *
18: * Phase order on entry:
19: *   IDLE -> LINK_DESCEND (64 frames) -> SWAP_ENTRY (1) -> IDLE.
20: * Phase order on exit:
21: *   IDLE -> SWAP_EXIT (1, instant) -> IDLE.
22: */
23:
