docs\superpowers\plans\2026-04-26-intro-title-screen.md:487:The 14-step palette progression `DemoPhase0Subphase1Palettes` (already transcribed in `extract_demo_palettes.py`'s `NES_CYCLES`) drives the fade. We need *all 64 Gen CRAM words per cycle* (not just 12 sprite-pal slots like the existing extract). And we need a compressed delay table summing to ~230 frames.
docs\superpowers\plans\2026-04-26-intro-title-screen.md:1085:NES `InitialTitleSprites` (Z_02.asm:342) lays out 28 sprites in 4-byte format `[Y, tile, attr, X]`. Genesis sprite list lives at the VDP sprite table (typically VRAM `$F800` for our setup) and uses 8-byte format `[Y, size+next, attr, X]` packed. Need to translate.
docs\superpowers\plans\2026-04-26-intro-title-screen.md:1098:For simplicity, fix Genesis sprite list at VRAM `$F800`. Set VDP register $05 to `$F800/$200 = 0x7C` to point sprite table there.
