docs\superpowers\specs\2026-04-30-roomrom-s1-sprite-link-design.md:86:**PAL3 conflict:** The BG renderer (`roomrom_ow_room_render_load_palette`) writes all four palette slots 0..3 from the NES level info, so PAL3 is currently a BG sub-palette. The fix is to modify the OW and UW BG palette loaders to write slots 0..2 only, freeing PAL3 for sprites. NES BG sub-palette 3 is rarely referenced in the OW/UW attribute tables; if any room shows a BG color regression after the change, that room will be flagged at verify and remapped in a follow-up. This is the long-term-correct split: BG owns PAL0..PAL2, sprites own PAL3.
docs\superpowers\specs\2026-04-30-roomrom-s1-sprite-link-design.md:99:- Position: room center, screen coords `(128, 88)`. SGDK applies sprite-table Y/X offsets internally; we pass screen-space.
