docs\plans\2026-05-27-cave-byte-exact-verification.md:3:**Goal:** Prove (or disprove) byte-for-byte that every cave $6A-$7D renders identical sprites + animation frames to NES Zelda 1 â€” via real NES-vs-Genesis OAM/PALRAM/CHR/animation-cadence byte-diff, not screenshot eyeballing.
docs\plans\2026-05-27-cave-byte-exact-verification.md:5:**Architecture:** Capture per-frame golden bundles from NES Z1 (NesHawk) at frames {0,8,16,24,60,120} per cave (covers bonfire 2-tile cycle + steady state). Capture same frames from Debug.md. Normalize NES 4-byte OAM â†’ Genesis 8-byte SAT + tile-id translate via MANIFEST.json + PALRAMâ†’CRAM via misc_palettes LUT. Byte-diff each domain. Every mismatch = a real bug to fix. Honest yes/no comes ONLY from the differ exit code.
docs\plans\2026-05-27-cave-byte-exact-verification.md:36:**Step 1: Write probe.** Per cave_id $6A..$7D: force cave mode (GameMode=$0B/$0C, RoomId=cave_id, ObjType+1=cave_id, NPC+bonfire slot positions per Z_01.asm:282 SetUpCommonCaveObjects), advance to stable, then capture OAM(256)+PALRAM(32)+CHR(8192) at relative frames {0,8,16,24,60,120}. FrameCounter $0015 forced to 0 at capture-start for determinism. Emit per-cave per-frame bundle.
