docs\SPEC.md:348:| T29 | File select | File select screen renders; can start Quest 1 | âš  In Progress (operational evidence is present via natural T30 flow: Mode `$01` and register mode `$0E` are observed before gameplay. Dedicated T29 refresh is still pending final threshold tuning; latest `builds/reports/bizhawk_t29_file_select_probe.txt` is 6/7 PASS with only `T29_NMI_CONTINUOUS` failing. Diary re-integration in merge `1e20d1c1 T27_T29 Phases 1+2+6+7 (Zelda27.48-27.56)`.) |
docs\SPEC.md:360:| T36 | Cave enter | Can enter first cave (room $76) and exit | Partial â€” 8/9 PASS (`bizhawk_t36_cave_parity_report.txt`). Enter / interior textbox / exit / round-trip all green. Residual `T36_CAVE_INTERIOR_MATCH` fails at t=307 with 1-frame obj-y phase offset: Gen runs sub=4 row-copy without frame-skip gate that NES has (finishes 2 frames early), Gen's sub=7 handler takes 2 frames longer than NES; net phase converges by t=308 with both platforms at (x=$70,y=$DB). Gameplay-correct; only strict-equality sampling at t=307 catches the transient. Three root-cause hypotheses disproved (Stage K MMC1 bank-window â€” `08bcc5fb`; Stage L T8 NMI cadence â€” `90a53d63`; Stage M T8-unrelated â€” `06701015`). Parked per stuck-rule. Separate issue: Room $76 *overworld* parity (left transition from $77) still fails `ROUTE_TRANSITION_SETTLE` â€” Genesis stalls at Mode 7 Sub 0 (EnterRoom init), NES advances to Mode 5. See `builds/reports/room76_parity_report.txt`. Orthogonal to T36 cave entry which uses the stairâ†’cave flow. |
docs\SPEC.md:384:| T38 | Enemy AI | Enemies spawn, move, and respond to hits | âš  Partial (2026-04-18) â€” edge-spawn rooms (bit 3 of `RoomAttrsOW_F`, ~20 OW rooms including $73/$74/$5B/$68) had all enemies stuck at Y=$DD with tile-check blocking every direction. Fix chain P42â€“P47 (`75602a8e`, `f9e9e9ed`): **P42** forces `AssignObjSpawnPositions` to run normal-spawn in OW (was short-circuiting for bit-3 rooms); **P43** adds UninitMonsterFromEdge fresh-room-entry gate (Codex-proposed â€” preserve SpawnPosList positions when `$004B=0`, `$000F=$FF`, residual X/Y non-zero); **P44** adds Gen-native `SpawnPosListPtrsGen` 32-bit pointer table (was indirecting NES $86xx â†’ Gen RAM $FF86xx = garbage); **P46** reseeds `CurEdgeSpawnCell ($0525)` to $48 (top-edge mid) on entry to edge-spawn rooms; **P47** pre-walk + post-walk $0525 validation â€” if FindNextEdgeSpawnCell walk terminates on bottom edge ($E0 hi-nibble) due to the corner boundary bug at $4F/$E0, snap to $48 and retry. Result at room $73 after 360 settle frames: Y=$DD count **0/12** (was 4/12 pre-fix); enemies in playfield 9/12, remaining 3 at Y=$3D top-edge walkable-down. |
