tools\probes\captures\_rev_gemini.txt:3:**BLOCKER** â€” **Underspecified Ground Truth / Contradictory Descent Mechanics** â€” The plan's "Context" states a "forced 64-frame walk-down descent (Link sinks behind the arch)," but the cited NES ground truth (`Z_05.asm:2308 UpdateMode10Stairs_Full`) for descent movement (`INC ObjY` every 4 frames) implies a total vertical travel of only 16 pixels over those 64 frames. This directly contradicts the spirit of a "64-frame descent" as a counterpart to the "48pxÃ—1fpp" ascend. This fundamental characteristic for the descent is either misstated or unverified for byte-exact parity.
tools\probes\captures\_rev_gemini.txt:4:**Fix:** Before Step 4, definitively clarify the exact total pixel movement and pixel-per-frame cadence for the descent, backed by specific ASM or an explicit NES probe capture. Update the plan's description of the descent to reflect this verified ground truth, noting any asymmetry with the 48px ascend if applicable.
